<title>USA: Koch Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>Koch Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Monday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $14.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $16.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $17.00</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
